@startuml control-lesson01-sequence
!theme plain
title Lesson 1: project test on the engine (Identify, Project experiment)
component "Control Studio page\nIdentify, method Project experiment\nReview project test → Confirm and start; Abort test" as page
component "Engine (trust-control-studio identify)\nreview: the identity of the campaign (loop revision, settings, declared 120.1 s, scenario)\nstart: the same identity, or refused; journaled before dispatch\nrecording with the program revision; restoration confirmed by an unforced scan\nanswer: kept recording and its samples, restoration, and the fit or its note" as engine
component "Runtime experiment service\ncontrol.experiment.* and control.recording.*\nP1.ExperimentEnabled (%MX24.0, BOOL): TRUE at start, FALSE at the end\nthe selected signals recorded with the program revision" as runtime
component "Lesson 1 ST\nfixed reference + measured-input validity\nexperiment update counter" as lesson
component "ColdStorageManualDemand\nON for 200 enabled updates (20 s)\nOFF afterward" as compressor
component "Door schedule\nopen at 60 s, closed at 90 s\nrelative to enablement" as door
component "One thermal state\nstate_space model\nindependent compressor / surroundings inputs" as room
component "Published temperature, door\nand surroundings observations" as observations

page --> engine : review, then start with the same identity\nAbort test: cancel of that operation
engine --> runtime : activation TRUE at start; recording of the selected signals
runtime --> lesson : P1.ExperimentEnabled\nexisting Boolean experiment path
lesson --> compressor : enable, validity, abort, counter
lesson --> door : same counter and enable conditions\n%QL16 DoorCommand: 1 while the door is open
compressor --> room : %QL0: OFF / ON encoding
door --> room : %QL8 SurroundingsCommand: 4 °C, 6 °C while the door is open
door --> observations : plant: %IL8 door indication\n%IL16 effective surroundings
room --> observations : %IL0: room temperature
observations --> runtime : recorded samples, with the program revision
runtime --> engine : restoration: activation FALSE, confirmed by an unforced scan
engine --> page : Project test completed. Outputs restored.\nkept recording and samples; the fit, or its refusal as the note
observations --> lesson : measured temperature validity only\nno temperature regulation

note bottom of lesson
Disabled, invalid or aborted: compressor OFF and door closed.
Restart simulator for a matching thermal initial state.
No activation-relative runtime event API is introduced.
end note

note bottom of engine
Normal completion restores the activation without asserting an abort.
Lesson 1 declares no abort binding, so an abort or a failed termination
restores the activation only (C12).
A fit that the recording cannot support is the test's note: the study keeps
the recording and no model, and its current model stays as it was (B3.7).
end note
@enduml
